{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And go for yourself to the land of Moriah.</b> He mentioned \"for yourself\" — that is, to your very essence, for from there come forth the materials [of the altar], which were taken from the place concerning which it is said (Exodus 20:21) ״מִזְבַּח אֲדָמָה תַּעֲשֶׂה לִּי״, as explained in parashat Lekh Lekha (Genesis 12:1). And in the word \"הַמּוֹרִיָּה\" the \"יָה\" appears superfluous, for it is said ״אֵלֶךְ לִי אֶל הַר הַמּוֹר״ (Song of Songs 4:6). Rather, it is because there is the place of the Foundation Stone, from which the two worlds were founded, which were created with the name יָהּ — for the gate of heaven is there, and there the union between the Holy One, blessed be He, and Israel is consummated, like the union of a husband with his wife in which the name יָהּ intervenes between them. And this will indicate its companion fifteen steps that were in the Women's Gallery, corresponding to the numerical value of the name יָהּ. And it was a sign for the Temple that would be built upon it after fifteen generations, from Abraham to Solomon." "And what He said, upon one of the mountains which I will tell you — for that place the Holy One, blessed be He, did not reveal to any creature, that upon it the Temple would be built, as its reason will be explained below in parashat Re'eh (Deuteronomy 12:4) with the help of HaShem; except for Abraham, who knew this secret, for therefore he called it \"YHWH will see,\" as will be explained nearby with the help of HaShem on the verse ״ה׳ יִרְאֶה״ (Genesis 22:14). Another matter: \"which I will tell you\" — for in the future the word of HaShem would come to His prophets from there, as it is written (Exodus 25:22) ״וְדִבַּרְתִּי אִתְּךָ מֵעַל הַכַּפֹּרֶת״. And some say \"which I will tell you\" refers to \"and offer him there for a burnt-offering\": He did not say \"and offer him [as] a burnt-offering\" but rather \"for a burnt-offering\" — that is, to offer up a different burnt-offering, which I will tell you — who the burnt-offering shall be: either your son or something else."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "The phrase רֵעוֹ חֲמֵשׁ עֶשְׂרֵה מַעֲלוֹת is translated as \"its companion fifteen steps,\" reading רֵעוֹ in the sense of a paired or corresponding feature; the reference is to the fifteen gradual steps in the Women's Court of the Temple (cf. Sukkah 5:4)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:29:01.103876726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}